From f69002a386762c21d29175d2a6461b1e0a2a551e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:22:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: build_evidence records each fill's real side, not
 hardcoded SELL (v0.14.1) (#11)

build_evidence() wrote every deal's exchange_side as a hardcoded "SELL",
silently correct only for a long-only consumer (momentum). Found while
scoping seykota's adapter -- seykota trades both directions (bot.py:
"SELL" if p.side == "long" else "BUY"), so a short position's real closing
fills are BUY-side, and the evidence would have permanently mislabeled them.

Now derives exchange_side from each normalized fill's own `side` field
(uppercased), falling back to "SELL" only when a caller's fills don't carry
one (backward compatible -- momentum's existing _precise_fill already
populates side correctly, so its output is byte-identical; no consumer needs
to change).

Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
